RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
November 10, 2008
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date at 6:00
p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR-Jack R. Spiker; COUNCIL MEMBERS-Mr.
Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins (arriving at 6:03 pm), Dr. Rinne, Mr. Segrave and
Mr. Valdez.   Absent: Mr. Laybourn, and Mr. Pierson.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Bob Nicholas,
Acting City Attorney.
Ms. Broyles recognized various community agencies and City departments as recipients
of 2008 Community Development Block Grant funding for programs and projects.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests, in which
event the item will be removed from the Consent Agenda and considered in its normal sequence
on the agenda.)  Mr. Valdez moved to approve Consent Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Segrave.
Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
OCTOBER 27, 2008.  Motion (per consent agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
NOVEMBER 3, 2008.  Motion (per consent agenda) carried.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Brown. Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
