```text
CORNER OF THE INTERSECTION OF STOREY BOULEVARD AND SYCAMORE
ROAD).”  Dr. Rinne declared a conflict of interest (nearby property owner interests) and vacated
Council Chambers.  Gloria Milmont commented on a letter she had sent to Council members and
expressed concerns with the property being zoned for commercial use in an established
residential neighborhood.  She advised she was not against the property owner’s proposed
business but is opposed to the recommended zoning classification, suggesting that a Mixed Use
Residential (MUR) zone would be a better option. Property owner Bob Parry requested action on
the item be postponed to provide his attorney the opportunity to review and provide legal
comment and analysis regarding the conditional zone restrictions approved at the last City
Council meeting.  Kathryn and Brent Kunz spoke in opposition to postponement.  Reporting for
Public Services Committee, Mr. Collins moved to approve on third and final reading, seconded
by Mr. Valdez.  Mr. Collins moved to postpone for two weeks (to Nov. 24, 2008), seconded by
Ms. Broyles.  Ms. Milmont indicated her support of a postponement if a MUR, instead of a
Neighborhood Business, zone would be considered during the postponement time frame.
Motion to postpone carried. Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present in
Council Chambers with the exception of Ms. Case and Mayor Spiker voting “no”.
“AN ORDINANCE AMENDING SECTIONS 2.04.040, 2.04.160 AND 2.04.170 OF
TITLE 2, ADMINISTRATION AND PERSONNEL, CHAPTER 2.04, MAYOR AND CITY
COUNCIL, OF THE CHEYENNE CITY CODE TO PROVIDE FOR A CLERICAL
CORRECTION, AND TO CLARIFY STATE LAW PROVISIONS CONCERNING
READINGS OF ORDINANCES AND REQUIRED VOTE.”  Mr. Collins raised a point of order
requesting action on the item be delayed until Dr. Rinne returned to Council Chambers with
Mayor Spiker concurring. Dr. Rinne returned to Chambers.  Mr. Collins moved to approve on
third and final reading, seconded by Ms. Broyles.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members
of the governing body present. (#3831)
“AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CERTAIN CHAPTERS AND SECTIONS OF TITLE
17, ZONING, OF THE CHEYENNE CITY CODE BY ADDING CHURCHES AS A USE
REQUIRING ADMINISTRATIVE APPROVAL IN THE FOLLOWING ZONE DISTRICTS:
NB-NEIGHBORHOOD BUSINESS DISTRICT, CB-COMMUNITY BUSINESS DISTRICT,
MUR-MIXED USE WITH RESIDENTIAL EMPHASIS DISTRICT, MUB-MIXED USE WITH
BUSINESS EMPHASIS DISTRICT, AND BY ADDING CHURCHES AS A USE
REQUIRING BOARD APPROVAL IN THE LI-LIGHT INDUSTRIAL DISTRICT.” John
Fafoutakis questioned local government involvement pertaining to zoning requirements for
church use.  Mayor Spiker stated the proposed changes to zoning regulations were requested by
the faith community, advising that some non-traditional places of worship are affected by zoning
regulations.  Mr. Collins moved to approve on second reading, seconded by Ms. Broyles.
Motion carried.  Voting “yes” - all members of the governing body present.
