```

### Page 5 of 7

```text
public availability, and commented on concerns with graffiti, as experienced in the downtown
parking structure, and adequate utilization of the new parking lot to uniformly benefit businesses
in the area.  Upon inquiry, Bob Bradshaw, Special Projects Director, reviewed the types of
parking anticipated to be available, and advised acquisition amount for the property is
$700,000.00 and excludes the cost of developing the lot.  Jay Harnish, owner, Ruby Juice;
Christian Cherek, Director, Downtown Development Authority; Jerry Innis, owner, Pizzeria
Venti; Gloria Milmont, resident, and Glen Garrett, architect, spoke in favor of the proposed
parking lot.  Topics discussed included: lack of dedicated parking on the east side of downtown;
parking lot benefit to existing and potential new businesses, downtown customers and residents;
2006 DDA parking study; past parking studies;  DDA goal to recruit dining and entertainment
operations on 17 St.; effects lack of parking has had on downtown businesses, and development
th
and character of the downtown area.  Mark Shubert spoke in opposition of property acquisition,
expressing his belief that service (privately owned) parking lots should be utilized.  Reporting
for Finance Committee, Mr. Segrave moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $700,000.00,
seconded by Mr. Collins.  Comments included: importance of downtown, improving parking
availability, previous parking studies indicating the need for more parking areas, and additional
parking contributing to economic development of downtown.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” –
all members of the governing body present in Council Chambers with the exception of Ms. Case
voting “no”. Following announcement of the vote, Ms. Broyles returned duties of the chair to
Mayor Spiker, who returned to Council Chambers.  (#5318)
[CA]
Memorandum of Understanding between the City of Cheyenne, Parks & Recreation
Dept., and the National Guard Bureau, for off-site pilot test at Mylar.  Motion (per consent
agenda) carried.  (#5319)
[CA]
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne, Parks & Recreation Dept., and Cheyenne
Artist Guild, for lease of the Carriage House located in Holliday Park.  Motion (per consent
agenda) carried.  (#5320)
CHANGE ORDERS/CONTRACT MODIFICATIONS:
Contract Modification No. 5 to Contract No. 3932 between the City of Cheyenne and
Voyageur Asset Management Inc., for a two year extension.  Mr. Segrave moved to approve,
seconded by Mr. Valdez.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body
present with the exception of Ms. Case voting “no”. (#3932)
Contract Modification No. 2 to Contract No. 5140 between the City of Cheyenne, Public
Works Dept., and Long Building Technologies, Inc., to add the Parks Maintenance Facility
located at 4500 Dell Range Blvd, Cheyenne, WY, to the Wyoming Energy Conservation
Improvement Program (WYECIP) Investment Grade Audit and Project Development.  Mr.
Segrave moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $1,680.00, seconded by Mr. Brown. Upon
inquiry, Vicki Nemecek, Public Works Dept., advised Parks and Recreation requested a review
of the building to determine ways to improve future energy conservation and efficiency.  Motion
carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present with the exception of Ms.
Case voting “no”.  (#5140)
