### Page 7 of 7

```text
OTHER CITY BUSINESS:
John Fafoutakis commented on concerns with overflowing community recycling bins.
Vicki Nemecek, Public Works Dept., expressed appreciation to the community for recycling
efforts; advised staff is working on an additional site to house bins for plastic, and confirmed the
blue bins are emptied daily, including Sunday.  Upon inquiry by Gloria Milmont, Mayor Spiker
explained recycling bins at the Transfer Station are located inside the gates for monitoring
purposes due to after hours depositing of items other than recyclable materials, and Ms.
Nemecek advised the recycling bins located at the north Albertson’s store have been temporarily
unavailable due to concrete construction pad work.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, the meeting was
officially adjourned at 7:06 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
November 19,  2008
